ck css-15maf5o" data-card-overlay-ui="true" contenteditable="false"><div class="css-17xejub"></div><div class="css-17xejub"></div></div><div dir="ltr" class="card-content is-full-width is-borderless" data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="card" style="whitespace:inherit"><div data-layout-item-id="body" class="react-renderer node-cardLayoutItem node-cardLayoutItem"><div dir="ltr" as="div" style="white-space:normal" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div data-content-reference="true" class="card-layout-cell-bg css-1jw19ud" data-selection-ring="true" data-selection-background="true"><div style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:100%" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="cardLayoutItem" style="whitespace:inherit"><div class="react-renderer node-heading animatable-on-load animatable-on-load-annotatable block block-heading first-block first-block-in-card"><div style="white-space:normal;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:var(--flex-align)" data-pos="13651" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" level="1" data-placeholder="Untitled card" class="heading themed-heading" style="white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:min(100%, 10em);align-self:var(--descendant-align-self, self-start)" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="heading" style="whitespace:inherit">Clinical Trial Participation in Neurotechnology</div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-paragraph animatable-on-load animatable-on-load-annotatable block block-paragraph"><div style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-pos="13700" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" style="white-space:pre-wrap" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="paragraph" style="whitespace:inherit">Clinical trials are the mechanism by which neurotechnology moves from laboratory to patient. Without them, devices cannot demonstrate safety and effectiveness, cannot achieve regulatory clearance or approval, and cannot become accessible through insurance reimbursement to the people who need them most.</div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-gridLayout block block-gridLayout"><div style="white-space:normal" data-pos="14005" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div class="grid-col-controls css-z1fkfg" data-selection-ring="true"><div class="layout-content" data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="gridLayout" style="whitespace:inherit"><div class="react-renderer node-gridCell animatable-on-load node-gridCell"><div class="grid-cell" data-pos="14006" style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-selection-ring="true" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="gridCell" style="whitespace:inherit"><div class="react-renderer node-heading animatable-on-load block block-heading first-block"><div style="white-space:normal;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:var(--flex-align)" data-pos="14007" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" level="4" data-placeholder="Heading 4" class="heading themed-heading" style="white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:min(100%, 10em);align-self:var(--descendant-align-self, self-start)" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="heading" style="whitespace:inherit">Why Clinical Trials Matter</div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-paragraph animatable-on-load block block-paragraph"><div style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-pos="14035" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" style="white-space:pre-wrap" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="paragraph" style="whitespace:inherit">New neurotechnology treatments do not become standard of care without a structured evidence base. Regulators require clinical evidence of safety and effectiveness before granting clearance or approval. Payers — including Medicare, Medicaid, and private insurers — require evidence of clinical benefit before covering a device or procedure.</div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-paragraph animatable-on-load block block-paragraph last-block"><div style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-pos="14376" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" style="white-space:pre-wrap" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="paragraph" style="whitespace:inherit">This is particularly consequential in neurotechnology, where the gap between promising research and accessible, reimbursed treatment has historically been wide. Enrollment in clinical trials is often the binding constraint on how fast the field can advance.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-gridCell animatable-on-load node-gridCell"><div class="grid-cell" data-pos="14636" style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-selection-ring="true" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="gridCell" style="whitespace:inherit"><div class="react-renderer node-heading animatable-on-load block block-heading first-block"><div style="white-space:normal;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:var(--flex-align)" data-pos="14637" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" level="4" data-placeholder="Heading 4" class="heading themed-heading" style="white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:min(100%, 10em);align-self:var(--descendant-align-self, self-start)" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="heading" style="whitespace:inherit">How Trials Are Regulated</div></div></div></div><div class="react-renderer node-paragraph animatable-on-load block block-paragraph"><div style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-pos="14663" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" style="white-space:pre-wrap" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="paragraph" style="whitespace:inherit">Clinical trials involving medical devices operate under a framework designed to protect participants and ensure the integrity of evidence. In the United States, this includes:</div></div></div></div><ul class="react-renderer node-bullet animatable-on-load block block-bullet" indent="0"><div dir="auto" style="white-space:normal" data-pos="14840" data-node-view-wrapper=""><li data-testid="bullet-list-item" data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="bullet" style="whitespace:inherit">FDA oversight including Investigational Device Exemption requirements for significant risk devices</div></li></div></ul><ul class="react-renderer node-bullet animatable-on-load block block-bullet" indent="0"><div dir="auto" style="white-space:normal" data-pos="14940" data-node-view-wrapper=""><li data-testid="bullet-list-item" data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="bullet" style="whitespace:inherit">Institutional Review Board review and approval</div></li></div></ul><ul class="react-renderer node-bullet animatable-on-load block block-bullet" indent="0"><div dir="auto" style="white-space:normal" data-pos="14988" data-node-view-wrapper=""><li data-testid="bullet-list-item" data-node-view-content="" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><div data-node-view-content-inner="bullet" style="whitespace:inherit">Federal rules governing informed consent under 21 CFR Part 50</div></li></div></ul><div class="react-renderer node-paragraph animatable-on-load block block-paragraph last-block"><div style="white-space:normal;position:relative" data-pos="15051" data-node-view-wrapper=""><div dir="auto" style="white-space:pre-wrap" data-node-view-content=""><div data-node-view-content-inner="paragraph" style="whitespace:inherit">Internationally, equivalent frameworks apply under the EU Clinical Trials Regulation, ICH Good Clinical Practice guidelines, and jurisdiction-specific requirements.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div contenteditable="fa